├── contact.html          <-- Page 4: Contact (Fixed Core)
├── menu-tool.html        <-- Page 5: Menu Builder (Client Tool Window)
├── shop-tool.html        <-- Page 6: Online Shop (Client Tool Window)
├── inventory-tool.html   <-- Page 7: Stock/Items (Client Tool Window)
├── news-tool.html        <-- Page 8: Announcements (Client Tool Window)
└── events-tool.html      <-- Page 9: Special Events (Client Tool Window)
Use code with caution.2. The Core Automation Engines (Open Code Elements)A. The Master Client Dashboard (/admin/index.html)Paste this code directly into your /admin/index.html file. This pulls in the open-source Decap CMS script via a free browser network (CDN), creating an instant login window for the business owner.html<!DOCTYPE html>
<html>
<head>
  <meta charset="utf-8" />
  <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0" />
  <title>Client Website Management Dashboard</title>
  <!-- Pulls the open CMS script into the browser safely -->
  <script src="https://unpkg.com@^3.0.0/dist/decap-cms.js"></script>
</head>
<body>
  <!-- Decap CMS injects the editing tools automatically right here -->
</body>
</html>
Use code with caution.B. The Automation Rules Engine (/admin/config.yml)This file tells the browser system exactly what parts of the 5 tool windows the client can change. It prevents them from breaking the core design while giving them full text control.yamlbackend:
  name: github
  repo: YOUR_GITHUB_USERNAME/YOUR_CLIENT_REPO_NAME
  branch: main

media_folder: "images/uploads"
public_folder: "/images/uploads"

collections:
  - name: "menu"
    label: "Restaurant Menu Items"
    folder: "data"
    extension: "json"
    create: true
    slug: "menu-item-{{slug}}"
    fields:
      - {label: "Dish Name", name: "title", widget: "string"}
      - {label: "Price", name: "price", widget: "string"}
      - {label: "Description", name: "description", widget: "text"}
      - {label: "Food Image", name: "image", widget: "image"}

  - name: "shop"
    label: "Online Shop Inventory"
    folder: "data"
    extension: "json"
    create: true
    slug: "product-{{slug}}"
    fields:
      - {label: "Product Name", name: "title", widget: "string"}
      - {label: "Price", name: "price", widget: "string"}
      - {label: "Stock Status", name: "status", widget: "select", options: ["In Stock", "Low Stock", "Out of Stock"]}
      - {label: "Product Image", name: "image", widget: "image"}
